ADR-075's residue experiment, kept so that a later row can rebuild it (Architect condition C3).

NOT SHIPPED. It neutralises the first four causes ADR-075 bisects, in the sim itself:
  1. the opening hand (MapData.PlaceSkirmishStart): the yard anchored so its footprint is the exact
     rotation, and the opening force mirrored in y as well as x;
  2. the free harvester (World.SpawnFreeHarvester): spawned at the cell centre beside the reflected corner;
  3. Fix64 multiplication (P8-53): truncated towards zero, as division already is;
  4. the production exit (World.ProductionSystem's SpawnOffsets): reflected, with the centre cell taken
     on the reflected side.
Each is a rule a human plays under, moves goldens and belongs to its own row (P8-62, P8-63, P8-53,
P8-64), so none of it may be merged as it stands.

Apply with: git apply docs/adr/ADR-075-residue-experiment.patch (it was cut against main after the
P8-21 pull request). The sheltered frame is the same build with the two comparisons in
SkirmishAI.TryFindPlacement reversed (2 * oax + anchorSize > w.Map.Width, and the same for the height).

Measured with it at seed 2026 (seatfairgate, pairs within 15 per cent of 16, mean gap, decided pairs by
start): this ADR's frame 13, 10.8 per cent, 8/5; the sheltered frame 14, 9.1 per cent, 6/5; the old
scan (SkirmishAI.cs restored to main) 9, 14.9 per cent, 8/5. mirrorprobe with this ADR's frame finds no
command difference before the first break on any two-seat map (first breaks t=406 to t=2493); with the
old scan the first placement differs on every map (t=210 Directorate, t=90 Sodality).

